// MUST FAIL: an enum declared with braces. Enums are brace-less in DESIGN.md
// without exception (392-398, 455-457, 500, 606, 641-645, 777-779, 819-821,
// 1027-1030). A braced body is a struct body, whose members are `name: T`,
// `name :: T`, or `name = sig` — `Circle(Circle)` is none of those.

Shape* = {
    Circle(Circle),
    Rect(Rect),
    Unit
}
